From: Gyimesi Balázs <gyimesi.balazs@gmail.com>
Subject: nss-gmac: use the GMAC as the parent device of the netdev

The netdev parent is set to the MDIO bus device, a workaround for a
phy_attach_direct() panic without a parent. The netdev is then not tied
to the DT node of its GMAC: a DSA switch looks up its conduit with
of_find_net_device_by_node(), never finds it, and its probe is deferred
forever. Use the GMAC platform device as the parent.

--- a/ipq806x/nss_gmac_ctrl.c
+++ b/ipq806x/nss_gmac_ctrl.c
@@ -1416,8 +1416,11 @@
 		}
 	}
 
-	/* workaround for tplink,onhub eth0 phy_attach_direct panic with poll enabled */
-	SET_NETDEV_DEV(netdev, gmacdev->miibus->parent); /* (netdev, &pdev->dev) ? */
+	/* phy_attach_direct() needs a parent device (it used to panic on the
+	 * tplink,onhub), and a DSA switch finds its conduit through the DT
+	 * node of the parent: use the GMAC platform device
+	 */
+	SET_NETDEV_DEV(netdev, &pdev->dev);
 
 	/*
 	 * Connect PHY
